 In the generated dashboard, the top KPI card section uses different types of micro-visualizations instead of putting the same mini-chart in every card.

1. Overdue — Alert / status micro-chart

Card contains:

Large number: 7 items

Red warning/exclamation icon inside a soft red circular background

Small comparison text: vs last 7 days

Red upward trend indicator: ↑ 16%


Visual purpose: Quickly tells the user that overdue work is increasing and needs attention.


---

2. On-Time Delivery — Target + trend indicator

Card contains:

Large KPI: 92%

Green check-circle icon

Supporting text: target 90%

Small green upward indicator: ↑ 4%


Visual purpose: Shows actual performance against a target.

You could make this more visually interesting with a small horizontal progress bar, for example:

██████████████████░░ 92%

with a thin marker at 90%.


---

3. Avg Utilisation — Mini radial gauge

This is probably the most useful alternative to the micro line chart.

Card contains:

Large KPI: 68%

Circular/radial gauge around the upper-right area

Gauge represents utilisation from 0–100%

Small text: of capacity 100%

Blue upward trend: ↑ 8%


Conceptually:

╭─────╮
      ╱         ╲
     │    ↗      │
      ╲         ╱
        ╰─────╯

Visual purpose: Immediately communicates how much capacity is being consumed.


---

4. WIP — Capacity progress bar

Card contains:

Large KPI: 19 items

Purple layers/stack icon

Text: limit 20

Horizontal progress bar

95% displayed beside the bar


Conceptually:

Limit 20

███████████████████░  95%
19 items

Visual purpose: Shows that WIP is very close to its maximum limit.


---

If you want different micro-charts in every card

For your dashboard, I'd recommend this combination:

Card	Micro-visual

Overdue	Mini sparkline + red alert icon
On-Time Delivery	Target progress bar
Avg Utilisation	Radial gauge
WIP	Capacity progress bar


This gives the KPI row visual variety without making it cluttered.

